PATCH 613: thread ES:BX and DS:SI through the reached 3318 callback (board:0034).

SOUNDDVR asm 014e:154-15b sets ES=CS (the sound overlay segment), BX=0x1cd, then FAR-calls
DGROUP:0x43e. The vector installed by section 0x1b8 reaches engine 3318. Engine asm
1000:331b-3320 sets DS=CS, SI=0x3bf1, then FAR-calls SS:0x32a. That target is 4ce7, whose
validated patch 012 takes encoded far ES:BX and DS:SI to splice a callback node. After
patch 612 fixed the far-vector address, calling it without these register inputs passed
native stack garbage / WASM undefined values. Thread both original far pointers explicitly.
The Oracle writes SOUNDDVR:0x1cd = `ea f6 3b 82 20` at 518.060 ms, i.e. the new node
inherits the old 2082:3bf6 link; the base-zero port must retain the same offset and
store the corresponding 0f69 segment. Evidence: scratch/sequence-capture/snd-node/mem.watch.txt.
